#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build next's tip for the owner's iPhone, ready for the Desktop installer (#384).

Usage:
  scripts/phone-build                 build the trunk's tip now (origin/main)
  scripts/phone-build --commit <sha>  build that commit instead
  scripts/phone-build --if-changed    coalesce changed tips to hourly (or sooner after integration PASS)
  scripts/phone-build --plan-only     rewrite latest's test-plan.md against the build installed now
  scripts/phone-build --source hosted take the GitHub-hosted build instead of building here (#2357)

Where the build comes from (#2357): `--source mac` (the default) builds here, as below. `--source hosted`, or
SM_PHONE_SOURCE=hosted, or the word `hosted` in ~/SpokenMargins-phone/source (so the launchd job switches
without a reinstall), runs no xcodebuild: it takes the newest unexpired artifact of a successful
.github/workflows/phone-build.yml run on the trunk (schedule or by hand), downloads it with `gh run download`,
gives it the same checks (provisioning profile, codesign --verify, commit in Info.plist) and writes the same
folder, build.json and test plan, so the Desktop installer is unchanged. Hosted builds come twice a day, before
the 8:00 and 17:00 Central plans; --if-changed takes a new one when it appears. Delete the file to build here again.

What it does:
- Builds a signed Release app for a physical iPhone in a persistent detached worktree, through
  scripts/xcodebuild-lane (so it waits for a Mac-wide build slot), with persistent Release DerivedData,
  automatic signing and -allowProvisioningUpdates. SM_BUILD_COMMIT puts the commit in the app's
  Info.plist, so Settings > Version names it once that key is on next.
- Output: ~/SpokenMargins-phone/<date-time>-<sha7>/ with the .app, build.json, build.log and
  test-plan.md, and a `latest` symlink to the newest good build. Keeps the three newest builds;
  older ones and temporary logs are deleted. .cache/src and .cache/dd-release stay at stable paths
  so unchanged source files and compiled intermediates can be reused by the next build.
- test-plan.md lists the listener-facing PRs merged since the build the owner last installed
  (~/SpokenMargins-phone/installed.txt, written by scripts/install-phone-build.command; a commit built
  on the Mac before it reached next still counts), each with
  its issue's "Owner check" line, sized to about ten minutes. A change whose issues are all closed
  is left out: the owner has passed it (#1100). Only written checks go in the ten minutes:
  a phone-found bug without one is listed with the other unchecked changes and the run names its issue
  (#847), and a check that names an issue or PR not on the phone yet waits in its own section. A step
  carries the check's own numbered steps, its URLs as links, and the repo files it names (copied to
  files/ and to iCloud Drive as "Test plan <sha7> files", beside the plan the installer puts there).
  A check that asks for a PDF, EPUB, audiobook or packet with no link and no repo file to attach waits
  with the run naming its issue (#1038); test PDFs live in TestPlans/phone-files/. So does a check that
  names a document with no link ("the arXiv paper") (#1476).
  A check the owner can't run isn't a check (#1476): one that names a script, simulator, commit to run at
  or log file (lane and agent procedures), reads a diagnostics field, or says to read an export or log without
  saying what it should show. The run names the issue whose "Owner check:" line needs rewriting, and a usable
  check elsewhere (the PR body) stands in. Three or more PRs changing the playback screen's view files are
  one item at the top of the ten minutes ("The playback screen changed"), each PR listed under its own title;
  PRs that share an issue keep their own titles in every list.
  After those, "Still waiting on your check" lists issues (open, or closed in the last 60 days: a merged fix closes its issue and the label stays) labelled `status: needs-human-validation` whose
  fix is in this build but wasn't in the changes above, for as long as nobody has checked them (#927). A check
  is read from the issue body or the PR as "Owner check", "Phone check" or a "## Steps" heading, and the newest
  one in the issue's comments wins, including the hourly dispatch's "This needs the owner's headphones: ...";
  a comment saying "Owner check: none" or "leave this off the owner's plans" keeps the issue out. They share the
  ten minutes with the new changes; the rest are listed with links. The current milestone's `priority` fixes
  lead, then its phone-found ones, and they keep their place however many new changes there are; one with no
  steps written yet is listed under "Important, but no phone steps written yet", never as nothing to test.
  `validate-by-use` fixes don't lead: his ordinary listening checks them.

Gates (hourly coalescing, #1329; bugs are fine, crashes the runners would catch are not):
- One phone build at a time (a lock in ~/SpokenMargins-phone). A second run exits at once.
- --if-changed starts at most once an hour, unless the current tip has an integration PASS on #184.
  Explicit builds without --if-changed bypass that delay. Deferred tips do not reset the hour.
- Memory pressure must be normal, and free disk at least 10 GB plus 4 GB per running build
  (counting this one). Otherwise it skips and exits 75; the next trigger tries again.
- Checks: a tip the lane runner pushed after testing it, or a safe re-merge of a tested PR (its
  "Merge check" names the resulting commit), has passed the lane's host-test gate; its author built
  both targets, and the iPhone build
  below compiles it again (the lane builds no app per PR since 2026-10-09). Any other commit (a
  merge by hand) gets `verify-tests.py --plan fast` and a simulator build-for-testing here first.
- A commit that failed once isn't retried by --if-changed; a newer tip is.
- The test plan has one record for the exact commit: app tests, Release device build, scripted journeys,
  attended journeys, upgrade and phone checks, each pass, fail or not run, plus every failure and
  exclusion the reports on #184 name (#1465).
- A failed Release build (the signed iPhone build or its checks) opens one item, "Release phone build is
  failing on next", naming the failed commit and the last good binary; another failing commit updates
  it, and the next Release success closes it. GitHub unreachable only skips the report.

The owner gets a macOS notification when a new build is ready, and when signing needs him (#500).

Environment (tests): SM_PHONE_DIR (default ~/SpokenMargins-phone), SM_PHONE_KEEP (3),
SM_PHONE_NOTIFY (the notification command, default osascript; `off` skips it),
SM_PHONE_DISK_FREE_GB (instead of measuring), SM_LANE_* (scripts/lane_slots.py, xcodebuild-lane),
SM_PHONE_GH (the gh command), SM_PHONE_NO_FETCH=1 (skip the fetch), SM_PHONE_REPO (the repo to
build from; default this checkout), SM_PHONE_ICLOUD (the iCloud Drive plans folder, as the installer).
Stdlib only, Python 3.9-compatible: launchd runs it under /usr/bin/python3.
"""
